            <ArticleTitle>Psychological management of anxiety and pain during dental treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>399-402</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sensation information, perceived control and distraction were compared with routine dentistry in a study of the effect of psychological context on pain and anxiety during dental treatment. The results indicated that the provision of sensation information was the most effective treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
